{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1450252-balanced-wyrm","id":1450252,"title":"Balanced Wyrm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-29T19:17:41-07:00","id":1450252,"title":"Balanced Wyrm?","content":"If Wyrm returns to Balance, or parts of that condition still exist, what does it look like? <br /> <br /> What\u2019s the difference between Balanced and Mad (aka. current) Wyrm? <br /> <br /> Will Shapeshifters or any other minion (spirits, supernaturals, etc.) follow him be marked as tainted too? <br /> <br /> What\u2019s the Gaian shapeshifters\u2019 attitude?<br /> <br /> <br /> Some materials I know:<br /> Rage Across Egypt has some balanced wyrmish spirits but they aren\u2019t welcome.<br /> <br /> One of ToJ scenarios \u201cWeaver rises\u201d may be helpful but I haven\u2019t read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T00:01:01-07:00","id":1450286,"title":"","content":"Weaver Ascendant describes what happens in broad detail if you manage to succeed at the rite to free the Wyrm. The tl;dr is that the energies immediately kill everyone in Malfeas and the cosmos is reordered hard before being allowed to slowly heal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T06:38:49-07:00","id":1450308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1450252-balanced-wyrm?p=1450286#post1450286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver Ascendant describes what happens in broad detail if you manage to succeed at the rite to free the Wyrm. The tl;dr is that the energies immediately kill everyone in Malfeas and the cosmos is reordered hard before being allowed to slowly heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Balanced Wyrm may exist all the time. For example Devil Tiger gui ren are thought to worship it, Rage Across Egypt also have balanced wymish spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T08:55:23-07:00","id":1450316,"title":"","content":"If the Wyrm returns to Balance it will generally mean a return to a sort of balance in the world so long as the Weaver and Wyld join in. Things are generated, take shape, and fall apart in due time. However imo the Triat can\u2019t really be restored fully to balance until humanity gets its shit together but if they returned to a mostly balanced form that would be a significant first step in the process (least of all because they\u2019re no longer actively sabotaging the project of human development).<br /> <br /> The current Wyrm still has manifestations of its original Balance Wyrm form. The Balance Wyrm is entropy in due time. Things grow old, fall apart, and die. They rot and decompose and lose form. They\u2019re returned to the ether and room is made for something new to rise into the absence. The Fallen Wyrm is about corruption. It\u2019s forcing the process of entropy by any means necessary. It\u2019s inciting violence and destruction to cause premature death and systems collapse. It\u2019s feeding into the spirit of extreme consumption without regard for restoration. It\u2019s facilitating the 101 ways a system can turn against its original purpose and become overly destructive. <br /> <br /> If the Wyrm was restored to its Balance Wyrm state then the fallen breeds would probably either be destroyed, abandoned, or saved in due time. As it stands one can respect and serve the interests of the Balance Wyrm currently but they shouldn\u2019t expect the Fallen Wyrm to offer them a ton of assistance unless they\u2019re willing to take some bane gifts in exchange for helping the Wyrm bust loose.<br /> <br /> Most of the Changing Breeds have been fighting the Fallen Wyrm for so long that the Balance Wyrm is going to be an alien concept to them outside of the oldest stories and theoretical notions. If the Fallen Wyrm was healed into the Balance Wyrm they\u2019d probably adapt and begin working on fixing the damage done and returning to a state of total balance so that they can return to their earliest states.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T18:32:03-07:00","id":1450527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1450252-balanced-wyrm?p=1450308#post1450308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Balanced Wyrm may exist all the time. For example Devil Tiger gui ren are thought to worship it, Rage Across Egypt also have balanced wymish spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, else freeing it wouldn't be possible.<br /> <br /> Freeing it is still a monumental feat that causes massive cosmic upheaval. That's why everyone in Malfeas dies from the magnitude of spiritual energies unleashed, and why the world gets a lot of cities and such blasted down into dust. That is the result of freeing the long-restrained force of pure balance and un-twisting the universe - everything gets reckoned all at once, and violently. Then, a lot of stillness, from which renewal can flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T06:18:29-07:00","id":1450581,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Balanced Wyrm can teach Gifts, what do they look like. Gryffon15\u2019s reply reminds me of Mage\u2019s Entropy Sphere.<br /> <br /> In my opinion:<br /> I also think three Triats of Wyrm may die, because that\u2019s the production of madness.<br /> <br /> All things about Corrupted Wyrm may meet something bad, for example vampires may perish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T14:28:23-07:00","id":1450641,"title":"","content":"From a practical perspective, Balance Wyrm is any entropic function normally found in nature. Detrivores, decomposers, or anything that decays or weakens life would be Balance Wyrm. These things recycle what currently exists into nutrients to be used for other life. If it is something you would normally find in nature that seems to meet the purpose of the Wyrm (destruction/entropy), you can assume it is &quot;Balance Wyrm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Corrupted Wyrm is for 1) any kind of supernatural evil (things that don't exist in the real world from a scientific point of view), 2) things that harm the world ecosystem that come from outside that normal system (it might come from space like asteroid impact or cosmic radiation that pierces Earth's magnetic field; it might originate deep within the Earth like massive volcanic eruptions spewing so much sulfur into the air it causes mass extinction; or man-made pollutants disrupting the ecosystem); or 3) evil that comes from the hearts of men, i.e. not things animals could do, but arise from humanity being sapient moral creatures who struggle with good and evil. Maybe's there more categories, but I think most things said to be &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; fall here.<br /> <br /> From a Garou philosophical or mythological point of view, the latter is a result of the Wyrm becoming &quot;corrupted&quot; or driven &quot;mad&quot; by the Weaver. Lots of players assume the Garou myths are correct and speculate how that can be changed.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I don't hold these anthropomorphic concepts of the Garou to be true. What Garou refer to as Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm are just the metaphysical trinity concepts of Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy. It's like taking things like Electromagnetism, Gravity, and the Nuclear Forces and assigning them personalities and actions. Balance Gravity is OK, but when a plane crash kills hundreds of people it's because of &quot;Corrupted Gravity&quot; and I want someone to blame. Boo, you terrible Corrupt Gravity! So the Garou created a mythology of the Wyrm going insane inside the Weaver's webs because it is their answer to the philosophical problem of Evil. <br /> <br /> Of course, there is an objectively true source of supernatural evil in the World of Darkness, and the powers of darkness are associated with a lot of things materially or philosophically entropic. So it's not a completely bonkers theory. But it's on the same path as saying evil exists because Satan rebelled against God; because an imperfect Demiurge made the world; there's a series of ever lesser perfect worlds in a metaphysical cycle of destruction and recreation; or that it is a result of desire in a world of illusion. In the World of Darkness, there are certainly powerful spirits that represent the mythology of Garou, but the same thing can be said for almost every human mythology and religion. Who's really right? In the end, it's only true if you as the ST want it to be true and assists in you making different decisions than you would if you held something else was true. Otherwise it's just fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T01:22:39-07:00","id":1451813,"title":"","content":"I found earliest edition Kitsune in Caern Places of Power follows Balanced Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T11:00:31-07:00","id":1451876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1450252-balanced-wyrm?p=1450641#post1450641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a practical perspective, Balance Wyrm is any entropic function normally found in nature. Detrivores, decomposers, or anything that decays or weakens life would be Balance Wyrm. These things recycle what currently exists into nutrients to be used for other life. If it is something you would normally find in nature that seems to meet the purpose of the Wyrm (destruction/entropy), you can assume it is &quot;Balance Wyrm.&quot;<br /> <br /> Corrupted Wyrm is for 1) any kind of supernatural evil (things that don't exist in the real world from a scientific point of view), 2) things that harm the world ecosystem that come from outside that normal system (it might come from space like asteroid impact or cosmic radiation that pierces Earth's magnetic field; it might originate deep within the Earth like massive volcanic eruptions spewing so much sulfur into the air it causes mass extinction; or man-made pollutants disrupting the ecosystem); or 3) evil that comes from the hearts of men, i.e. not things animals could do, but arise from humanity being sapient moral creatures who struggle with good and evil. Maybe's there more categories, but I think most things said to be &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; fall here.</div> </div> </div> </div>#1 is iffy, #2 definitely isn't the case, since Rorg likes to chuck asteroids but isn't corrupted and Helios isn't either, in spite of bathing the solar system in all kinds of ionizing radiation. #3 is also subverted on occasion by the existence of one-off monsters, non-human fomori, and other strangeness. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a Garou philosophical or mythological point of view, the latter is a result of the Wyrm becoming &quot;corrupted&quot; or driven &quot;mad&quot; by the Weaver. Lots of players assume the Garou myths are correct and speculate how that can be changed.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I don't hold these anthropomorphic concepts of the Garou to be true. What Garou refer to as Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm are just the metaphysical trinity concepts of Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy. It's like taking things like Electromagnetism, Gravity, and the Nuclear Forces and assigning them personalities and actions. Balance Gravity is OK, but when a plane crash kills hundreds of people it's because of &quot;Corrupted Gravity&quot; and I want someone to blame. Boo, you terrible Corrupt Gravity! So the Garou created a mythology of the Wyrm going insane inside the Weaver's webs because it is their answer to the philosophical problem of Evil.<br /> <br /> Of course, there is an objectively true source of supernatural evil in the World of Darkness, and the powers of darkness are associated with a lot of things materially or philosophically entropic. So it's not a completely bonkers theory. But it's on the same path as saying evil exists because Satan rebelled against God; because an imperfect Demiurge made the world; there's a series of ever lesser perfect worlds in a metaphysical cycle of destruction and recreation; or that it is a result of desire in a world of illusion. In the World of Darkness, there are certainly powerful spirits that represent the mythology of Garou, but the same thing can be said for almost every human mythology and religion. Who's really right? In the end, it's only true if you as the ST want it to be true and assists in you making different decisions than you would if you held something else was true. Otherwise it's just fluff. </div> </div> </div>W:tA is, we are told from an omniscient narrator's point of view, an animist horror reality. If everything has a spiritual reflection, why would the most widespread and essential forces be exempt? The universe doesn't rush to bend to Garou beliefs (this isn't Mage, after all), they were just born here and caught up in a twisted cosmos.<br /> <br /> The problem of the Corrupter Wyrm and the Maddened Weaver also goes beyond simple casualties or inconvenience; the former has a drive to ruin without renewal and commit an extroverted cosmic suicide for its failures, while the latter wants to freeze the cosmos to completely inspect it so that it can know everything, as mysteries exist beyond even it, and it doesn't like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}